–.7)\n        │  WireGuard (wg-opdbus, 10.0.0.0/24) — decoy only, never on the host\n        ▼\n┌──────────────────────── DECOY  129.80.64.127 (Oracle) ─────────────────────────┐\n│ enp0s6 10.0.1.17  gw 10.0.1.1     wg-opdbus 10.0.0.1     wg0 10.10.0.0/24      │\n│ Browser TLS terminates here (10.0.0.1); OIA1 issuer :51888                     │\n│ Admin SSH entry 10.0.0.1:2222 (bound to wg-opdbus) → 127.0.0.1:2222            │\n│ Xray REALITY server \"egress-reality\" :9443 → 127.0.0.1:443, cover name         │\n│   assistant.ghostbridge.tech, ML-DSA-65 signed                                 │\n│ netns op-warp: official WARP/MASQUE client → 162.159.198.2 udp 443 (+500,4500…)│\n│   warp-uplink 192.168.253.1/30 (carrier)   warp-data 192.168.252.1/30 + v6 (data)│\n│ Policy: prio 10 → table 28051 (10.0.0.2/32, 10.0.0.3/32 via rtly-lungs)        │\n│         prio 40 → 28050 underlay exceptions   prio 200 → 28053 rest via warp-data│\n│         mark 0x51820 → 51820 (wgcf-ingress)                                    │\n│ rtly-lungs (TUN 5, MTU 1280): 192.168.255.2  peer 10.0.0.2                     │\n└───────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────┘\n   SSH -w 5 as warp-link to 188.68.58.237:2223          reverse admin SSH\n   (carried in MASQUE via Cloudflare; SSH protects      (host dials out as\n    the payload from Cloudflare)                         ubuntu@129.80.64.127)\n                │                                              │\n┌───────────────▼────────────── HOST  \"3tched\"  188.68.58.237 ─▼──────────────────┐\n│ eth0 ── OVS uplink, no address                                                  │\n│ ovsbr0 (OVS, standalone, MTU 1420)                                              │\n│   ├─ pub0 (internal)  188.68.58.237/22  gw 188.68.56.1  — public address only   │\n│   ├─ ovsbr0 aliases: EMQX 10.0.0.3 · OpenFlow (unassigned) · Qdrant (unassigned)│\n│   └─ tun5/rtly-lungs as a persistent port (owner decision 10-05)               │\n│ rtly-lungs (TUN 5, persist, owner warp-link): 10.0.0.2 peer 192.168.255.2       │\n│   + REALITY/transport address; prio 10 → table 28051 (10.0.0.0/25, .128/25)     │\n│ sshd #2 (op-warp-ssh-host) :2223 — warp-link only, PermitTunnel p2p, no shell   │\n│                                                                                 │\n│ Door:   op-grpc-bridge  10.0.0.2:8090  tonic TLS (svc0 local-CA cert)           │\n│         interceptor: OIA1/SID1 → anchor_verified_human_session                  │\n│ Web:    op-web 10.0.0.2:8080 (gRPC-Web → door); page 10.0.0.4 (now on ovsbr0)   │\n│ MQTT:   EMQX 10.0.0.3          tched-router (threetched) 127.0.0.1:8084         │\n│ Xray:   native, Unix sockets only under /run/ghostbridge/xray/                  │\n│         uds-xray-reality publishes :8444 → reality.sock (decoy XHTTP → .2:8444) │\n│ Admin:  127.0.0.1:22 ← decoy reverse tunnel; public :22 until cut over          │\n│ Firewall: nftables (filter only, never NAT); admits :2223 and rtly-lungs input  │\n│                                                                                 │\n│ Containers: no NIC, no IP. One socket: /run/opdbus/lungs/lungs.sock             │\n│   → guest /run/3tched-lungs.socket; kernel peer-cred auth per call;             │\n│   3tchedFS mounts /run/mount/3tchedFS in the guest (/run/mounts/3tchedFS host)  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Traffic paths**\n\n| Flow | Path |\n|---|---|\n| Browser → app | client → WireGuard → decoy (TLS ends at 10.0.0.1) → table 28051 → rtly-lungs → MASQUE/SSH TUN → host 10.0.0.2:8090/8080 → interceptor |\n| Admin SSH | client → WireGuard → 10.0.0.1:2222 → decoy loopback → reverse tunnel → host 127.0.0.1:22 |\n| Decoy egress | everything else → warp-data → Cloudflare (NAT happens only inside the namespace) |\n| Host egress via Xray | host HTTP socket → REALITY client → decoy :9443 |\n| Container → control plane | process → lungs.sock (D-Bus,