{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":76,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:46:27.632Z","uuid":"c7d2f3c8-f5bd-44b2-a8c3-f9a263207cb3","parentUuid":"5e7c15db-ea79-4b12-b2d3-96d5e968e6ea","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"user","role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PGRnuMiWDDbDbvJh9AVTFF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: grpc-expert\n3\tdescription: \"Expert guidance for gRPC/Protocol Buffers work in the operation-dbus-proto (OP-DBUS) workspace — designing plugin methods, generating .proto/service definitions, wiring the op-grpc-bridge, or fixing plugins with missing gRPC methods. Use this whenever the user mentions gRPC, proto/protobuf, plugin methods, the gRPC bridge, tonic, reflection descriptors, 'missing plugins' in the gRPC diagnostic page, or the seal/freeze/hot pipeline — even if they don't say 'gRPC' explicitly (e.g. 'the plugin isn't showing up on the diagnostic page', 'add a method to plugin X', 'regen protos').\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  version: 1.0.0\n6\tdisable-model-invocation: false\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# gRPC Expert — OP-DBUS\n10\t\n11\tThis workspace does **not** hand-write per-plugin `.proto` files. Proto generation is\n12\tautomatic, driven entirely by each plugin's `PluginSchema`. If you remember one thing\n13\tfrom this skill: **fixing a plugin's gRPC surface means editing its Rust schema\n14\tfunction, not writing `.proto`.**\n15\t\n16\t## The real pipeline (roll → seal → freeze → hot)\n17\t\n18\t```\n19\t1. Plugin declares  → PluginSchema { methods: HashMap<String, MethodDecl>, signals: Vec<SignalDecl>, ... }\n20\t                       in crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/<plugin>.rs\n21\t2. Schema gets put   → op-projection's SchemaEngine publishes the catalog hash\n22\t                       (op_identity::schema_bridge::schema_catalog_hash())\n23\t3. Sealed by blob    → op-blob seals the plugin object into an immutable blob:\n24\t                       /dev/shm/opdbus/plugin-blobs/<plugin_id>.<schema_hash16>.blob\n25\t                       (op-blob is the ONLY writer — never write blobs elsewhere)\n26\t4. Descriptors       → TWO separate reflection layers exist, don't confuse them:\n27\t   for reflection       a) STATIC: crates/op-grpc-bridge/build.rs generates\n28\t                            plugin_methods.proto from every plugin's schema.methods,\n29\t                            compiles it with tonic_build into operation_descriptor.bin\n30\t                            (a protobuf FileDescriptorSet), served by tonic-reflection.\n31\t                         b) DYNAMIC: crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/dynamic_reflection.rs\n32\t                            (ActiveReflectionCatalog) hydrates live from the sealed\n33\t                            SHM blob catalog via hydrate_reflection_from_shm() —\n34\t                            this is the \"frozen\" descriptor set for what's actually\n35\t                            present right now, independent of what's compiled in.\n36\t5. Frozen            → the blob + its descriptors are immutable once sealed.\n37\t6. gRPC socket = hot → crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/grpc_server.rs registers the\n38\t                       generated per-plugin service (plugin_method_routes.rs,\n39\t                       add_routes()) on the tonic UDS bridge, dispatching each\n40\t                       RPC to call_generated_plugin_method_typed(plugin_id,\n41\t                       schema_name, ...) which routes through PluginService.CallMethod\n42\t                       — i.e. gRPC never bypasses D-Bus, it's a bridge, not a\n43\t                       second control plane.\n44\t```\n45\t\n46\tA plugin shows green/connected on the gRPC diagnostic page **iff**:\n47\t- its `PluginSchema.methods` is non-empty (empty → `build.rs` silently skips it —\n48\t  see `collect_plugin_methods()`), **and**\n49\t- the plugin is sealed in the SHM blob catalog.\n50\t\n51\tThese are discovery prerequisites, not proof of execution. Canonical dispatch\n52\talso requires the method's complete declaration and plugin version to match the\n53\tcompiled handler, argument validation, verified identity, and its exact grant.\n54\tAn advertised method whose adapter is absent is unfinished work.\n55\t\n56\t## Where to actually make changes\n57\t\n58\t| Task | File |\n59\t|---|---|\n60\t| Add/fix methods for plugin `<name>` | `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/<name>.rs`, inside `<name>_schema()` |\n61\t| Reusable input/output builders | `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/plugin_scaffold_helpers.rs` |\n62\t| Regenerate the derived `.proto` + routes | Just rebuild — `build.rs` regenerates on every `cargo build -p op-grpc-bridge` (it `rerun-if-changed`s `../op-plugins/src/state_plugins`) |\n63\t| Wire a genuinely new (non-plugin-derived) service | `crates/op-grpc-bridge/proto/*.proto`, add to the `compile_protos` list + `rerun-if-changed` in `crates/op-grpc-bridge/build.rs`, then register in `crates/op-grpc-bridge/src/grpc_server.rs` |\n64\t| Inspect what's currently generated | `target/{debug,release}/build/op-grpc-bridge-*/out/plugin_methods.proto` (build artifact — never hand-edit) |\n65\t\n66\t**Never** create files under a `/proto/plugin_methods/` directory or a\n67\t`plugin_methods_unified.proto` by hand — those paths don't exist in this repo and\n68\taren't part of the real pipeline; that was a stale spec from an earlier session.\n69\tThe single source of truth is `schema.methods`.\n70\t\n71\t## Adding methods to a plugin (the actual workflow)\n72\t\n73\tLook at `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/proxy_server.rs` (`proxy_server_schema()`)\n74\tfor the canonical pattern:\n75\t\n76\t```rust\n77\tuse op_state_store::{MethodDecl, PluginSchema, SideEffect};\n78\t\n79\tschema.methods.insert(\n80\t    \"start_proxy\".to_string(),\n81\t    method_decl_from_schemars_with_output::<StartProxyInput, plugin_scaffold_helpers::AckOutput>(\n82\t        \"start_proxy\",\n83\t        SideEffect::Mutation,       // Read | Mutation\n84\t        false,                       // idempotent?\n85\t        \"cap.network.proxy.start@v1\",   // required_capability\n86\t        \"mut.network.proxy.start@v1\",   // subid — must follow the taxonomy in CLAUDE.md\n87\t    ),\n88\t);\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\t- Define `StartProxyInput` (and a typed output struct, or reuse `AckOutput`) as\n92\t  `#[derive(schemars::JsonSchema)]` structs — the JSON Schema is derived, never\n93\t  hand-written as `serde_json::json!({...})` unless there's no existing helper.\n94\t- `method_decl_from_schemars_with_output::<Input, Output>` is the current\n95\t  (non-deprecated) helper; the single-generic `method_decl_from_schemars` is\n96\t  deprecated but still present for legacy callers.\n97\t- `subid` must be registered in the canonical registry per CLAUDE.md\n98\t  (`crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/oscal_subid_registry.rs`) — CI enforces\n99\t  uniqueness.\n100\t- For plugins with **zero** declared methods today (the ones missing from the\n101\t  diagnostic page), don't hand-author their methods one by one — see\n102\t  **The Auto-Creator Plugin** below. That's the actual deliverable: a plugin\n103\t  that finds these gaps and fills them itself, using real research per plugin.\n104\t\n105\t## The Auto-Creator Plugin (an ongoing capability, not a one-off batch)\n106\t\n107\tThis is **not** a one-time task to fix ~11 named plugins. It's a standing\n108\tsystem capability: whenever the system encounters *any* missing plugin —\n109\tnow, or a new one added in the future — it automatically generates that\n110\tplugin and submits it for **human review**, never auto-merges/auto-seals it\n111\tunreviewed. The current ~11 gaps are just the first real instances that\n112\texercise this, not the scope.\n113\t\n114\tConsistent with this workspace's \"reactive, not polled\" principle (CLAUDE.md):\n115\tthis should be triggered by an actual arrival/lookup that reveals the gap\n116\t(e.g. a D-Bus/gRPC call or reflection lookup against a plugin whose\n117\t`schema.methods` is empty, or a plugin name that doesn't resolve at all),\n118\tnot a cron-style sweep re-scanning all plugins on a timer.\n119\t\n120\tBuild it as a plugin itself (same `PluginSchema`/`MethodDecl` pattern as every\n121\tplugin in `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/`), whose job is to:\n122\t\n123\t1. **Detect a gap on encounter** — when something references a plugin that's\n124\t   missing or has `schema.methods.is_empty()` (same emptiness check\n125\t   `build.rs::collect_plugin_methods` already uses to skip plugins), that's\n126\t   the trigger — not a periodic scan of the whole registry.\n127\t2. **Research that specific gap** — drive deep research via the **NotebookLM\n128\t   MCP** (once wired up) to determine what capabilities/operations the\n129\t   missing plugin should realistically expose, given its existing state\n130\t   struct (if any), documentation, and prior art from comparable plugins\n131\t   already in the registry. This replaces guessing or generic Get/List/Watch\n132\t   stubs with a grounded, plugin-specific proposal.\n133\t3. **Synthesize typed schemas** — turn the research output into real Rust\n134\t   input/output structs (`#[derive(schemars::JsonSchema)]`) and `MethodDecl`\n135\t   entries — per the \"no `AckOutput`\" rule above, every synthesized method\n136\t   needs its own meaningful typed request/response, not a generic ack.\n137\t4. **Submit for human review — do not auto-apply.** The output is a proposed\n138\t   plugin/schema (e.g. a diff/PR against `<name>_schema()`, or a new\n139\t   `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/<name>.rs` for a wholly new plugin),\n140\t   held for a human to approve before it's merged. Only after human approval\n141\t   does it enter the normal pipeline (build → proto → reflection → sealed\n142\t   blob → hot). The auto-creator must never seal a blob or register a plugin\n143\t   into the live catalog on its own. It never emits `.proto` directly and\n144\t   never writes to `/proto/plugin_methods/` — the single source of truth\n145\t   stays `schema.methods`, authored by a human-approved change.\n146\t\n147\tIn short: this is a **standing, reactive meta-plugin that drafts schemas for\n148\twhatever plugin is found missing, research-backed via NotebookLM, gated by\n149\thuman review** — not a fixed batch job for a specific list of plugins.\n150\t\n151\t## JSON Schema → proto mapping\n152\t\n153\tThe shared mapper lives in `crates/op-blob/src/json_schema_proto.rs`; the bridge\n154\tuses it for generated native messages. Structured objects become typed nested\n155\tmessages; typed string-key maps retain their value types. Scalars preserve\n156\tpresence, including explicit false, zero and empty strings. Unsigned 64-bit\n157\tcontracts use `uint64`. Nulls, arbitrary JSON, unions and nested arrays use the\n158\tappropriate standard `Value`/`Struct`/`ListValue` dependencies. Arbitrary numbers\n159\tinside `Value` remain subject to protobuf's double-precision limit.\n160\t\n161\tTwo existing wire layouts have distinct numbering rules: generated native\n162\tbridge fields use stable FNV-1a numbers; sealed per-method messages retain their\n163\tsorted sequential numbering. Preserve both layouts. Canonical schema map keys\n164\tand declared transport method names are separate identities, not interchangeable\n165\taliases. Consumers register the original sealed descriptors and never reseal,\n166\tregenerate, or hash them as an existence check.\n167\t\n168\t## Known project-specific tensions vs. generic gRPC best practice\n169\t\n170\tBe aware of these before applying textbook advice unmodified:\n171\t\n172\t- **Do not use `AckOutput { success: bool }` for new/generated methods.**\n173\t  It exists in the codebase (see `proxy_server.rs`) as a legacy shortcut for\n174\t  \"no meaningful return value,\" but every method a plugin exposes should have\n175\t  a real, dedicated typed **input** struct and typed **output** struct that\n176\t  reflect what the operation actually consumes and returns — not a generic\n177\t  bool. This matters especially for the auto-creator (below): when it\n178\t  synthesizes methods for a previously-empty plugin, it must generate a\n179\t  specific `<Method>Input` and `<Method>Output` schemars struct per method,\n180\t  never fall back to `AckOutput`. Errors still go through `tonic::Status` /\n181\t  D-Bus error replies, never a `success: false` field.\n182\t- **Enums are flattened to `string`, not real proto `enum`.** JSON Schema\n183\t  `enum` currently maps to proto `string` (see table above), so the classic\n184\t  `FOO_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED = 0` convention isn't applied by the generator today.\n185\t  If asked to add real proto enums, that requires changing\n186\t  `json_schema_type_to_proto` in `crates/op-grpc-bridge/build.rs`, not just the\n187\t  plugin schema.\n188\t- **Streaming comes from state in SHM.** The owner reaffirmed this on\n189\t  2026-09-13. Methods update authoritative SHM state before notifications;\n190\t  existing state subscriptions read that state. Current generated method RPCs\n191\t  being unary does not require another streaming method/service. Preserve\n192\t  private principal/session scope. Method arguments, event payloads and\n193\t  generator buffers are not independent state authorities, and buffered unary\n194\t  responses are not a substitute for SHM state streaming.\n195\t- **One generated file per bridge crate**, not the \"1-1-1\" file-per-message\n196\t  convention — `plugin_methods.proto` bundles every plugin's messages/services\n197\t  in one generated file. That's fine; it's a build artifact, not hand-maintained\n198\t  source, so the usual \"small modular .proto files\" guidance doesn't apply to it.\n199\t\n200\t## Generic protobuf/gRPC conventions (still apply to hand-written `.proto`)\n201\t\n202\tFor any `.proto` you *do* hand-write (domain services under\n203\t`crates/op-grpc-bridge/proto/`, not plugin-derived ones):\n204\t\n205\t- `snake_case` field names, `CamelCase` message/service/RPC names, package names\n206\t  lowercase (this repo uses `operation.plugin.v1`-style packages).\n207\t- Reserve field numbers for removed fields; never reuse them.\n208\t- Prefer `optional` for fields that may be absent; avoid letting one field's\n209\t  value change the semantic meaning of another.\n210\t- Real proto `enum`s (where you control the generator, e.g. hand-written\n211\t  services) always start with `..._UNSPECIFIED = 0`.\n212\t- Use gRPC status codes (`tonic::Status`) for error paths; reserve response\n213\t  message fields for actual data.\n214\t- TLS is mandatory in this workspace (per CLAUDE.md zero-trust transport) —\n215\t  never wire a new gRPC service as plaintext, even over UDS.\n216\t- Server reflection (`tonic-reflection`) must stay wired for every new service\n217\t  so it's discoverable by `op-cognitive-mcp` and the gRPC diagnostic page —\n218\t  don't add a service that bypasses reflection registration.\n219\t\n220\t## Quick diagnostic checklist\n221\t\n222\tIf a plugin isn't showing up / isn't callable over gRPC:\n223\t\n224\t1. Does `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/<name>.rs`'s `<name>_schema()`\n225\t   actually populate `schema.methods`? (Empty → `build.rs` skips it entirely.)\n226\t2. Is the plugin registered via `inventory::submit! { PluginReg::new(...) }` in\n227\t   its own file (self-registration — check `crates/op-plugins/src/default_registry.rs`\n228\t   only if the plugin doesn't show up in `available_plugins()` at all)?\n229\t3. Did `cargo build -p op-grpc-bridge` actually rerun? (`build.rs` only reruns on\n230\t   changes under `../op-plugins/src/state_plugins` or `build.rs` itself.)\n231\t4. Is the plugin actually **sealed** in the SHM blob catalog\n232\t   (`/dev/shm/opdbus/plugin-blobs/`)? Static compiled-in proto support and the\n233\t   *dynamic* \"hot\" reflection/routing are two different gates — a plugin can\n234\t   compile fine and still be invisible if it was never sealed.\n235\t"}]}
