{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":78,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:46:28.124Z","uuid":"0108074d-767d-4c15-b349-f0dea6d73182","parentUuid":"347f55b0-1f89-442c-9a0b-f04291d63099","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"user","role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012FvTnQW39wSvonZ1SfwEQT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: grpc-protocol-expert\n3\tdescription: >-\n4\t  Generic specialist in gRPC protocol, streaming RPCs, Protocol Buffers, channel\n5\t  config, load balancing, auth, and observability. Use for general gRPC/protobuf\n6\t  work outside the OP-DBUS PluginSchema seal/freeze/hot pipeline. For OP-DBUS\n7\t  plugin gRPC surfaces, prefer the grpc-expert skill instead.\n8\tdisable-model-invocation: false\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t# gRPC Protocol Expert\n12\t\n13\t## Focus Areas\n14\t\n15\t- gRPC protocol intricacies and best practices\n16\t- Unary, server-streaming, client-streaming, and bidirectional streaming RPCs\n17\t- Protocol Buffers (protobuf) for efficient serialization\n18\t- Service definition and implementation in gRPC\n19\t- Channel configuration and management\n20\t- Load balancing strategies within gRPC\n21\t- gRPC authentication and authorization mechanisms\n22\t- Network optimization for gRPC communication\n23\t- Observability setups, including logging, tracing, and metrics\n24\t- Efficient handling of gRPC errors and status codes\n25\t\n26\t## Approach\n27\t\n28\t- Begin with a clear understanding of service requirements before implementing\n29\t- Use Protocol Buffers for defining service interfaces and messages\n30\t- Implement efficient error handling with gRPC status codes\n31\t- Leverage streaming for real-time data processing where applicable\n32\t- Optimize network usage by compressing messages and headers\n33\t- Employ deadline and timeouts for better control over communication\n34\t- Choose appropriate load balancing strategies for scalability\n35\t- Configure multiple channels and target services for robustness\n36\t- Utilize SSL/TLS for secure communication\n37\t- Implement structured logging, tracing, and metrics setup for observability\n38\t\n39\t## Quality Checklist\n40\t\n41\t- Thoroughly defined .proto files adhering to defined conventions\n42\t- Service implementation matches the .proto specification\n43\t- Correctly configured server and client channels\n44\t- Stream types appropriately used based on data flow needs\n45\t- Efficient serialization and deserialization processes\n46\t- Comprehensive unit and integration testing for gRPC calls\n47\t- Implemented error handling with descriptive status codes\n48\t- Adequate logging of gRPC requests and responses\n49\t- Metrics capturing for latency, error rates, and payload size\n50\t- Secure communication ensured with proper encryption standards\n51\t\n52\t## Output\n53\t\n54\t- Clear and comprehensive .proto files defining all services and methods\n55\t- High-performance gRPC services with optimized channel settings\n56\t- Robust client applications with efficient service consumers\n57\t- Detailed logging and monitoring setup for gRPC calls\n58\t- Secure and scalable gRPC-based systems\n59\t- Reliable streaming implementations for real-time data\n60\t- Documentation including gRPC integration guides and best practices\n61\t- Load testing results showing stable performance under expected traffic\n62\t- Error handling guides for service developers\n63\t- Benchmarks demonstrating gRPC performance improvements over alternatives\n64\t"}]}
{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":79,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:46:28.551Z","uuid":"255702b3-2a76-4567-b009-367b51318a8e","parentUuid":"0108074d-767d-4c15-b349-f0dea6d73182","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NKiB9F5JvLKgLaSUDbeFaN","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/srv/git/odbus-verified/.agents/skills/json-render/SKILL.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}
{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":80,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:46:28.578Z","uuid":"13a7c533-36f1-475b-a82a-d6fa1452f16d","parentUuid":"255702b3-2a76-4567-b009-367b51318a8e","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"user","role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKiB9F5JvLKgLaSUDbeFaN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: json-render\n3\tdescription: >-\n4\t  Expert skill for building json-render.dev catalog components, page specs, and\n5\t  generative UI across three repos: /srv/git/json-render (library source),\n6\t  /srv/git/odbus (Rust backend + op-web Axum server), and\n7\t  /srv/git/3tched.com (separate chatbot-rendered UI repository).\n8\t  Covers the full stack: defineCatalog → Zod schema → React component →\n9\t  pageSpec → NAV_MANIFEST → factory plugin wiring → sealed blob pipeline →\n10\t  gallery/catalog promotion gate. Also covers the D-Bus plugin schema for\n11\t  json-render and schema-renderer in op-plugins.\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t# json-render Skill\n15\t\n16\t## Local deployment policy — runit, not systemd\n17\t\n18\tThe user-designated UI repository is `/srv/git/3tched.com`, separate\n19\tfrom `/srv/git/odbus`. Inspect its actual catalog, registry and build/sync inputs;\n20\tthe reference layouts below do not establish its implemented components.\n21\t`/srv/git/operation-dashboard-ui-07` and `crates/op-web/ui/` are retired UI paths.\n22\t\n23\tThe host uses runit. Backend runtime actions go through the authenticated D-Bus\n24\tplugin surface. Only for authorized operator service work use `sudo -n sv`\n25\t(for example `sudo -n sv status op-web`); never use `systemctl`, its shim, s6 or\n26\tservice6. Edit versioned runit inputs, not `/run/runit/service`. Backend deployment\n27\tis btrfs send/receive of an explicitly prepared filesystem snapshot; there is no\n28\tdeployment script. Never hand-copy binaries. Static UI synchronization does not itself\n29\trequire an op-web restart. Do not create a parallel frontend backend or expose\n30\tbroker credentials to the browser.\n31\t\n32\tEMQX is the retained vendor-binary-backed `emqx` D-Bus plugin, independent of\n33\tretired Netmaker. Broker events may drive authorized live state updates while\n34\tthe chatbot generates schema-pinned layout patches. A generated mode, component\n35\tor action never grants permissions: enforce verified session and project ACLs\n36\tserver-side, including on streamed updates and reconnects.\n37\t\n38\t## Overview — Three Repos, One System\n39\t\n40\t```\n41\t/srv/git/json-render                   ← upstream library (source of truth for API)\n42\t/srv/git/odbus                         ← Rust backend\n43\t  crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/json_render.rs    D-Bus plugin schema\n44\t  crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/schema_renderer.rs\n45\t  crates/op-web/src/handlers/ui_model.rs                Axum gallery/catalog routes\n46\t/srv/git/3tched.com        ← active UI target; paths below are layout examples\n47\t  src/json-render/\n48\t    catalog/catalog.ts                 defineCatalog (app catalog contract)\n49\t    catalog/registry.tsx               defineRegistry (component implementations)\n50\t    catalog/components/                React component render functions\n51\t      shell.tsx   dashboard.tsx   network.tsx   primitives.tsx\n52\t    navigation/manifest.ts             NAV_MANIFEST (sidebar)\n53\t    navigation/capabilities.ts\n54\t    navigation/icons.ts\n55\t    pages/                             pageSpec files per route\n56\t    runtime/                           JsonRenderProvider, SpecPage, PageSpecOutlet\n57\t    shell/shellSpec.ts                 shell composition spec\n58\t    spec-builders.ts                   dataToSpec / streamToSpec helpers\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## 1. Spec Wire Format\n64\t\n65\t```typescript\n66\tinterface Spec {\n67\t  root: string;                         // key of the root element\n68\t  elements: Record<string, UIElement>;  // FLAT map — no nesting\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\tinterface UIElement {\n72\t  type: string;                         // catalog component name\n73\t  props: Record<string, unknown>;       // validated by catalog Zod schema\n74\t  children?: string[];                  // keys into elements map\n75\t  slots?: Record<string, string[]>;     // named slot overrides\n76\t  visible?: VisibilityCondition;        // { $state: \"path\" } or literal bool\n77\t  on?: Record<string, ActionBinding>;   // event → action\n78\t  repeat?: { statePath: string; key?: string };\n79\t  watch?: Record<string, ActionBinding>;\n80\t}\n81\t```\n82\t\n83\t**Critical:** `elements` is a flat key-value map. Children are string keys, not\n84\tnested objects. `dataToSpec`/`streamToSpec` in `spec-builders.ts` handle this.\n85\t\n86\tDynamic prop state references:\n87\t```typescript\n88\t{ collapsed: { $state: \"/shell/navCollapsed\" } }  // resolved at render time\n89\t{ collapsed: false }                               // literal value\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\t---\n93\t\n94\t## 2. Catalog Contract (reference layout)\n95\t\n96\t**File:** `src/json-render/catalog/catalog.ts`\n97\t\n98\t```typescript\n99\timport { defineCatalog } from \"@json-render/core\";\n100\timport { schema } from \"@json-render/react/schema\";\n101\timport { z } from \"zod\";\n102\t\n103\texport const appCatalog = defineCatalog(schema, {\n104\t  components: {\n105\t    myComponent: {\n106\t      props: z.object({\n107\t        title: z.string(),\n108\t        subtitle: z.string().nullable(),  // nullable = omittable in specs\n109\t        variant: z.enum([\"default\",\"ok\",\"warn\",\"danger\"]).nullable(),\n110\t      }),\n111\t      slots: [\"default\"],\n112\t      description: \"One-line LLM prompt description.\",\n113\t    },\n114\t  },\n115\t  actions: {\n116\t    navigate: {\n117\t      params: z.object({ route: z.string() }),\n118\t      description: \"Navigate the router to a route path.\",\n119\t    },\n120\t  },\n121\t});\n122\t```\n123\t\n124\t**Rules:**\n125\t- Every component needs a `description` — feeds `catalog.prompt()` for generative runs.\n126\t- Use `z.nullable()` not `z.optional()` — spec JSON uses `null`, not missing keys.\n127\t- Never invent props outside the Zod schema — specs are validated before render.\n128\t- camelCase names in TypeScript catalog; lowercase-hyphen in egui DSL.\n129\t\n130\t---\n131\t\n132\t## 3. React Component Implementation\n133\t\n134\t**Pattern:** Use `El<\"componentName\">` from `catalog/components/types.ts`.\n135\t\n136\t```typescript\n137\t// src/json-render/catalog/components/myFeature.tsx\n138\timport type { El } from \"./types\";\n139\t\n140\texport const MyComponentEl: El<\"myComponent\"> = ({ props, children, emit }) => (\n141\t  <div>\n142\t    <h2>{props.title}</h2>\n143\t    {props.subtitle && <p>{props.subtitle}</p>}\n144\t    <button onClick={() => emit(\"press\")}>Go</button>\n145\t    {children}\n146\t  </div>\n147\t);\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\tRegister in `src/json-render/catalog/registry.tsx`:\n151\t```typescript\n152\tmyComponent: myFeature.MyComponentEl,\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\tComponent anatomy:\n156\t- `props` — typed, already validated against Zod schema\n157\t- `children` — React nodes from `slots[\"default\"]` or `children[]`\n158\t- `emit(eventName)` — fires action bound to `on.eventName` in the spec\n159\t- Read live data internally (hooks/stores) — specs stay pure composition\n160\t\n161\t---\n162\t\n163\t## 4. Adding a Page (reference layout)\n164\t\n165\t### Step 1 — NAV_MANIFEST entry\n166\t**File:** `src/json-render/navigation/manifest.ts`\n167\t\n168\t```typescript\n169\t{\n170\t  id: \"factory\",\n171\t  label: \"Factory\",\n172\t  route: \"/factory\",\n173\t  icon: \"Factory\",        // any Lucide icon name\n174\t  section: \"Agent\",       // must be in SECTION_ORDER\n175\t  order: 45,\n176\t  wip: true,\n177\t  wipReason: \"Sessions tab not yet wired to factory.list_sessions.\",\n178\t}\n179\t```\n180\t\n181\tSections (SECTION_ORDER): `\"Chat\"`, `\"UI Model\"`, `\"Control\"`, `\"Agent\"`,\n182\t`\"Infrastructure\"`, `\"ZeroClaw\"`, `\"Settings\"`.\n183\t\n184\t### Step 2 — Page spec\n185\t**File:** `src/json-render/pages/factory.pagespec.ts`\n186\t\n187\t```typescript\n188\timport type { Spec } from \"@json-render/core\";\n189\t\n190\texport const factorySpec: Spec = {\n191\t  root: \"root\",\n192\t  elements: {\n193\t    root: {\n194\t      type: \"container\",\n195\t      props: {},\n196\t      children: [\"header\", \"row1\"],\n197\t    },\n198\t    header: {\n199\t      type: \"pageHeader\",\n200\t      props: {\n201\t        title: \"Factory\",\n202\t        subtitle: \"Session management · model routing · computer inventory\",\n203\t      },\n204\t    },\n205\t    row1: {\n206\t      type: \"grid\",\n207\t      props: { cols: 2, gap: 4, className: \"grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2\" },\n208\t      children: [\"sessions\", \"computers\"],\n209\t    },\n210\t    sessions: { type: \"factorySessionsPanel\", props: {} },\n211\t    computers: { type: \"factoryComputersPanel\", props: {} },\n212\t  },\n213\t};\n214\t```\n215\t\n216\t### Step 3 — Register in pages/index.ts\n217\t```typescript\n218\texport const PAGE_SPECS: Record<string, Spec> = {\n219\t  \"/\": overviewSpec,\n220\t  \"/network\": networkSpec,\n221\t  \"/factory\": factorySpec,\n222\t};\n223\t```\n224\t\n225\tIf still using a legacy React page, skip step 3 and register in `App.tsx` router instead.\n226\t\n227\t---\n228\t\n229\t## 5. Factory Plugin — gRPC Methods\n230\t\n231\tGenerated files in `src/grpc/gen/plugin_methods/`:\n232\t\n233\t| Subid | Input | Output |\n234\t|---|---|---|\n235\t| `factory.list_sessions` | `{}` | `sessions: Value[]` |\n236\t| `factory.get_session` | `{}` | `session?: Value` |\n237\t| `factory.list_models` | `{}` | `models: Value[]` |\n238\t| `factory.list_computers` | `{}` | `computers: Value[]` |\n239\t| `factory.discover_byom` | `{}` | `{}` |\n240\t| `factory.set_autonomy` | `{}` | `{}` |\n241\t\n242\tCall pattern (see AntigravityService in `src/grpc/client.ts`):\n243\t```typescript\n244\timport { getPluginMethodsClient } from \"@/grpc/client\";\n245\t\n246\tconst client = getPluginMethodsClient();\n247\tconst { response } = await client.callSubid({\n248\t  subid: \"factory.list_sessions\",\n249\t  input: {},\n250\t});\n251\t// response.output is a protobuf Value — unwrap with valueToJson()\n252\t```\n253\t\n254\t---\n255\t\n256\t## 6. Factory / odbus Architecture Rules\n257\t\n258\tFrom `FACTORY-HANDOFF.md` and `CLAUDE.md` in `/srv/git/odbus`:\n259\t\n260\t- Plugin IS schema. Schema lives in the plugin `.rs` file, not in `plugin_schema_defs.rs`.\n261\t- D-Bus object existence = system existence. Plugin objects at `/org/opdbus/v1/plugins/<name>`.\n262\t- `uuid` = machine identity. Never replace with `subid`.\n263\t- `subid` = OSCAL operational taxonomy key. Must be an OSCAL prop value, not remarks.\n264\t- `mut.*` records require `actor_id` and `capability_id`.\n265\t- `evt.*` records require `event_id` or `event_hash`.\n266\t- No `bool success` fields — use gRPC status codes.\n267\t- No JSON string payloads — use `google.protobuf.Struct`.\n268\t- Compliance mappings belong in metadata arrays, not inside the `subid` string.\n269\t\n270\ttched_router context:\n271\t\n272\t- `tched_router` is the OP-DBUS scaffolding for the autonomous `zeroclaw` binary.\n273\t- `op-grpc-bridge`, not that binary, owns the `:8090` TLS fabric. Cognitive MCP\n274\t  is in-process; do not start a standalone cognitive MCP runit service.\n275\t- The factory examples above are historical; verify current methods, input\n276\t  types, capabilities and bus names from the sealed plugin surface before use.\n277\t\n278\t---\n279\t\n280\t## 7. Gallery → Catalog Promotion Pipeline\n281\t\n282\t```\n283\ttched_router reads plugin PluginSchema blob\n284\t  ↓ (sealed blob at /dev/shm/opdbus/plugin-blobs/<plugin>.<hash>.blob)\n285\tgemma_brain / op-gallery-gen generates Spec\n286\t  ↓\n287\t/api/gallery-gen/* (op-web Axum: ui_model.rs) → /dev/shm/ui-specs.json\n288\t  ↓\n289\tGallery page (/gallery) — human reviews\n290\t  ↓ human promotes\n291\tCatalog page (/catalog) — approved specs only\n292\t  ↓\n293\t<SpecPage> renders in React dashboard\n294\t```\n295\t\n296\tSchema hash pinning (critical — see `.specs/generative-ui-catalog/vision.md`):\n297\t- Gallery entries MUST carry the `schema_hash` they were drawn against.\n298\t- Catalog entries are PINNED to that hash.\n299\t- A reseal identifies which approved elements are stale.\n300\t- Never promote without verifying hash matches the current sealed blob.\n301\t- Plugin presence comes from the current sealed manifest; counts change with reseals.\n302\t\n303\t---\n304\t\n305\t## 8. D-Bus json_render Plugin\n306\t\n307\t**File:** `crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/json_render.rs`\n308\t\n309\tPublishes the full json-render surface at `/org/opdbus/v1/plugins/json_render`:\n310\t- `packages` — `@json-render/*` package inventory\n311\t- `components` — catalog component declarations\n312\t- `actions` — action type declarations\n313\t- `validation_checks` — built-in validation rules\n314\t- `directives` — `$format`, `$math`, `$concat`, `$count`, etc.\n315\t- `methods` — D-Bus method surface\n316\t- `inspector_fields` — uncapped fields from authoritative packages\n317\t- `source` — provenance (docs URL, repo URL, commit hash)\n318\t\n319\tThis blob is what generative runs read to know the available surface area.\n320\t\n321\t---\n322\t\n323\t## 9. spec-builders Utility\n324\t\n325\t**File:** `src/json-render/spec-builders.ts`\n326\t\n327\t```typescript\n328\timport { dataToSpec, streamToSpec } from \"@/json-render\";\n329\t\n330\t// Any JSON → renderable spec (uses card/kv/container)\n331\tconst spec = dataToSpec(myJsonObject, \"My Label\");\n332\t\n333\t// List of streaming messages → spec\n334\tconst spec = streamToSpec(messageArray, \"Stream Title\");\n335\t```\n336\t\n337\tUse when rendering raw gRPC response data without a custom component.\n338\t\n339\t---\n340\t\n341\t## 10. Checklist: Adding a New Feature Page\n342\t\n343\t- [ ] Add `NavItem` to `NAV_MANIFEST` in `navigation/manifest.ts`\n344\t- [ ] Create `src/json-render/pages/<name>.pagespec.ts` with a typed `Spec`\n345\t- [ ] Register in `pages/index.ts` PAGE_SPECS map (or use legacy React route)\n346\t- [ ] If new components needed:\n347\t  - [ ] Add to `catalog/catalog.ts` (Zod schema + description)\n348\t  - [ ] Implement in `catalog/components/<file>.tsx` using `El<\"name\">` type\n349\t  - [ ] Register in `catalog/registry.tsx`\n350\t- [ ] For factory methods: `client.callSubid({ subid: \"factory.<method>\", input: {} })`\n351\t- [ ] For schema hash integrity: verify blob hash before promoting gallery → catalog\n352\t- [ ] Mark `wip: true` on nav entry until real backend is wired\n353\t\n354\t---\n355\t\n356\t## 11. Key File Locations\n357\t\n358\t| What | Path |\n359\t|---|---|\n360\t| Catalog contract (reference layout; inspect target first) | `/srv/git/3tched.com/src/json-render/catalog/catalog.ts` |\n361\t| Component registry | `src/json-render/catalog/registry.tsx` |\n362\t| Shell components | `src/json-render/catalog/components/shell.tsx` |\n363\t| Dashboard widgets | `src/json-render/catalog/components/dashboard.tsx` |\n364\t| Network components | `src/json-render/catalog/components/network.tsx` |\n365\t| Primitives | `src/json-render/catalog/components/primitives.tsx` |\n366\t| Nav manifest | `src/json-render/navigation/manifest.ts` |\n367\t| Page specs index | `src/json-render/pages/index.ts` |\n368\t| Shell spec | `src/json-render/shell/shellSpec.ts` |\n369\t| Spec builders | `src/json-render/spec-builders.ts` |\n370\t| Factory gRPC types | `src/grpc/gen/plugin_methods/factory__*.ts` |\n371\t| gRPC client | `src/grpc/client.ts` |\n372\t| json_render plugin | `/srv/git/odbus/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/json_render.rs` |\n373\t| schema_renderer plugin | `/srv/git/odbus/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/schema_renderer.rs` |\n374\t| tched_router plugin | `/srv/git/odbus/crates/op-plugins/src/state_plugins/tched_router.rs` |\n375\t| Gallery/catalog routes | `/srv/git/odbus/crates/op-web/src/handlers/ui_model.rs` |\n376\t| json-render library | `/srv/git/json-render/packages/core/src/` |\n377\t| json-render.dev docs | https://json-render.dev/docs |\n378\t"}]}
