{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":123,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:47:19.596Z","uuid":"3a8c5127-0b8c-4a67-beb3-7602a41567ff","parentUuid":"28d9c3a1-3f21-4ef3-82a8-b9d1b085f1ae","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"user","role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VoB1KPeQEVKeWNRvLv3Wwq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 3tched restoration handoff — 2026-10-14\n2\t\n3\tWritten from Jeremy's laptop session (Claude Code) before moving the work onto the VPS.\n4\tFull plan: `RESTORATION-PLAN.md` beside this file (the laptop copy, newer than\n5\t`/root/system-restoration-20261013/RESTORATION-PLAN.md`). Status below was observed on the VPS\n6\ton 2026-10-14 between 10:40 and 15:10 UTC.\n7\t\n8\t## Owner decisions made today\n9\t\n10\t- **Target is this VPS** (`3tched`, Devuan 6, runit). Not the laptop.\n11\t- **Root overlay, two slots.** Two system-wide release overlays rotate per release; keep only\n12\t  *active* and *previous*; no release history. Only releases install into the\n13\t  overlay; everything else installs onto the base system. The latest release stays active\n14\t  across reboots until the next release.\n15\t- **Golden script stays** (`deploy/runit/build-golden.sh`) as the way releases are prepared.\n16\t  Golden has not been implemented on this fresh system yet (`/opt/op-dbus/golden` is empty).\n17\t  Its tree is laid out for `/opt/op-dbus/current`, not `/` — `bin/`, `sbin/` would be hidden\n18\t  by the base's `/bin`/`/sbin` symlinks and `opt/...` hidden by the `/opt` mount. Layout for a\n19\t  root overlay still to be decided.\n20\t- **op-storage's golden code is not used for releases** (it keeps multiple release versions).\n21\t  It is uncommitted (not in the GitHub repo); copies exist only in\n22\t  `/srv/git/odbus-btrfs-enforcement-20261013` and the installed daemon, which still serves\n23\t  hourly snapshots.\n24\t- **Qdrant is part of the release.**\n25\t- **EMQX stays in `/opt`** (base system), not in the release.\n26\t- **ZeroClaw → `threetched`**: install upstream ZeroClaw, rename the binary to `threetched`.\n27\t  **No patches** — `vendor/tched-router/patches/*` are deprecated (our code is separated from\n28\t  upstream; it should be plain upgrades). The patches may have caused earlier bugs.\n29\t  Config directory goes in `/opt` and is the only place that keeps the ZeroClaw name\n30\t  (proposed `/opt/zeroclaw`; upstream reads `ZEROCLAW_CONFIG_DIR`). Old config exists at\n31\t  `/home/jeremy/.zeroclaw` (Aug, 588K).\n32\t- The repo will be **pulled**, not copied from the laptop.\n33\t\n34\t## Findings\n35\t\n36\t1. **Hourly snapshots stalled since 2026-10-14 02:00Z.** That run published set\n37\t   `4883943c-142e-481b-9b09-09440684db43` (all 7 members), then the hourly cleanup of the previous set\n38\t   deleted the old `home` snapshot and got `EPERM` on `logs` (subvolume 270). `pending.json`\n39\t   (phase `retiring_previous_host_set`) now blocks every run (\"Prior run is incomplete\").\n40\t   op-storage *is* in the trusted guard cgroup (`/opdbus-storage`, id 6364, both FSIDs), has\n41\t   full caps, no file attributes, no default-subvolume involvement. Leading hypothesis: a\n42\t   concurrent `btrfs send` of that snapshot (kernel returns EPERM for delete-during-send);\n43\t   not proven. The guard did deny 212 native btrfs ioctls from untrusted callers (counter 0).\n44\t2. **Ownership change at 07:48Z** (owner did it deliberately, now says put it back):\n45\t   `/opt` (and much of `/home`, `/var/log`, `/srv/git`, `/var/lib/cargo-build`, some of `/`)\n46\t   was chowned to jeremy. op-storage requires root-owned, non-group/world-writable ancestors\n47\t   for its destinations: `/opt`, `/opt/op-dbus`, `/opt/op-dbus/system-snapshots/*`,\n48\t   `/opt/op-dbus/send`, `/opt/op-dbus/vector-store` (+`timing`, `vectors`, `.writer.lock`),\n49\t   `/opt/op-dbus/vector-captures`, `/opt/op-dbus/development-checkpoints`.\n50\t   The 02:00Z snapshot set holds the pre-chown owners/modes. A read-only comparison ran at\n51\t   14:57Z; per-member lists are in `/root/ownership-restore-20261014/` (`*.restore.tsv` =\n52\t   back to 02:00Z owner/mode, `*.new.tsv` = created after 02:00Z, no record). Restore counts:\n53\t   `/` 1, `/opt` 33, `/home` 5, `/var/log` 71, `/srv/git` 4,367, cargo-build 20,935, golden 1.\n54\t   Nothing has been changed yet.\n55\t3. **Old system content copied into `/opt` at 06:05:26Z** (after the 02:00Z snapshot): the fresh\n56\t   `/opt` held only `nodejs` and `op-dbus` (root-owned). Added: antigravity-ide, audit, btmp,\n57\t   claude-code, critical, emqx (link), emqx-6.2.2, emqx-6.2.2-c5b549…, google,\n58\t   google-cloud-cli, Grok Bot, oci-cli, op-mcp-providers, opdbus, opt, pacman.log, telnet,\n59\t   wtmp, Zenflow (~5.8 GB). Sources exist on the recovery disk (`p3-btrfs/@/opt`,\n60\t   `vdb-p2/@/opt`). Owner keeps EMQX; the rest is undecided.\n61\t4. **EMQX**: the system uses `emqx-6.2.2-c5b549d312d…` (version + SHA-256 pin in\n62\t   `deploy/config/emqx.version`). `emqx-6.2.2` is a byte-identical duplicate. `/opt/emqx`\n63\t   currently points at nonexistent `/opt/op-dbus/current/opt/emqx`. Both copies' `etc` →\n64\t   `/etc/emqx`, which does not exist; user `emqx` and an `emqx` runit service do not exist.\n65\t5. **threetched build**: a patched build was started then stopped at owner's direction; no\n66\t   processes remain. Leftovers: partial cache `/var/lib/cargo-build/threetched-cache`, empty\n67\t   `/var/lib/cargo-build/odbus-verified/threetched-artifacts/tched-router`.\n68\t6. Other: backend never built (only `op-storage` in the release target; baseline build exit\n69\t   101 on missing threetched input). `mdadm` runit service flaps (enabled, `/etc/sv/mdadm`\n70\t   missing). `/opt/op-dbus/current` → nonexistent `releases/…-e46dad8`. No network topology\n71\t   (only eth0): no OVS/WG/Xray/WARP/incus. Two Qdrant instances: 6343 (runit\n72\t   `qdrant-drive-recovered`, `/mnt/qdrant-drive-recovery`, 26 collections, verified docs\n73\t   round-trip, full snapshot sha `bce23c66…`) and 6335 (manual, root, recovery-disk\n74\t   `overlay-work/qdrant-run`, go/python/c/java/docs + 430k rust_lang_rust).\n75\t   Reboot validation still outstanding.\n76\t\n77\t## Voice over SSH (set up today)\n78\t\n79\t`vps-voice` on the laptop reverse-forwards the laptop's PipeWire-Pulse socket to\n80\t`~/.pulse-laptop/native` on the VPS. Installed `libasound2-plugins libsox-fmt-pulse\n81\tpulseaudio-utils`; `~/.asoundrc` (ALSA default → pulse) and `~/.config/pulse/client.conf`\n82\tfor root and jeremy (originals backed up as `*.before-voice-20261014` if present — none were).\n83\tVerified `arecord`/`rec` capture the laptop mic. `xcb_connection_has_error` noise comes from\n84\t`DISPLAY=:20` in jeremy's rc files; harmless, or start with `DISPLAY= claude`.\n85\t\n86\t## Open questions for the owner\n87\t\n88\t- Ownership restore scope (everything vs `/opt` + storage paths) — then finish the\n89\t  interrupted hourly cleanup and clear `pending.json`.\n90\t- Remaining old `/opt` content: remove or keep.\n91\t- Golden layout for a root overlay; where Qdrant live data lives (read-only release layer).\n92\t- Which Qdrant data set becomes the release copy (6343, 6335, or merge).\n93\t- ZeroClaw upstream version to install (pin was v0.8.4, commit a56c345d…).\n94\t\n95\t## Update 15:25Z — hourly snapshots unblocked by hand; permanent fix still needed\n96\t\n97\t- Ownership put back to `root:root` (modes unchanged) on the 18 paths op-storage manages:\n98\t  `/opt`, `/opt/op-dbus`, `golden`, `send`, `development-checkpoints`, `vector-captures`\n99\t  (+ `capture-616299d0…`), `vector-store` (+ `.writer.lock`, `timing`, `vectors`),\n100\t  `system-snapshots` + its 6 member dirs. Before-state:\n101\t  `/root/ownership-restore-20261014/by-hand-before-20261014T151218Z.tsv`. Everything else\n102\t  left as is (cleanup later, per owner).\n103\t- Interrupted cleanup finished by hand (6 calls); only set `4883943c` remains (all 7 members);\n104\t  `pending.json` cleared; `last.json` marks \"manual reconciliation\" at 15:13:44Z.\n105\t- **Root cause:** op-storage `delete_by_id` (`crates/op-storage/src/engine.rs`, NativeBackend)\n106\t  calls `btrfs_uapi::subvolume::subvol_sync_wait_one` after each `subvolume_delete_by_id`.\n107\t  That is `BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SYNC_WAIT` (ioctl 65). Kernel 6.12.111 does not implement it\n108\t  (UAPI header stops at 64; nothing in kallsyms), and the guard denies the unknown encoding\n109\t  even for the trusted cgroup → EPERM. The delete itself succeeds, so every call removed one\n110\t  member and then failed. Guard counters confirmed one denial per deletion.\n111\t- **Next hourly run (16:00Z) will stall again** after deleting one old member.\n112\t- **Fix (owner said \"whatever you think is right\"):** remove the `subvol_sync_wait_one` call\n113\t  from `delete_by_id` in the VPS source `/srv/git/odbus-btrfs-enforcement-20261013/crates/op-storage`\n114\t  (the running binary 4039cec2… was built from it; the laptop copy is older — ignore it).\n115\t  The existing readback (`child(...).is_none()`) already verifies removal. Then rebuild,\n116\t  install to `/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-storage/op-storage`, update its line in\n117\t  `manifest.sha256` (bootstrap check verifies all 7 hashes), `sv restart op-storage`, and\n118\t  run `/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-storage/op-storage-hourly` once to prove a full cycle.\n119\t  Allowing ioctl 65 in the guard would not help on this kernel.\n120\t\n121\t## Kernel plan (owner, 15:30Z)\n122\t\n123\tOwner will upgrade to the **XanMod** kernel first, then fix hourly cleanup. Consequences:\n124\t`/usr/local/libexec/opdbus-storage/bootstrap-check.sh` pins `uname -r` = `6.12.111+deb13-amd64` and\n125\tthe BTF sha256, so the guard service (and op-storage behind it) will refuse to start on the new\n126\tkernel until the guard is rebuilt (`/root/btrfs-enforcement-20261013/kernel-guard/build.sh`\n127\tregenerates the allowlist from the new UAPI/BTF), the pins and `manifest.sha256` are updated, and\n128\tthe guard is reloaded (stop op-storage, `guardctl mode off`, `guardctl unload`, start guard service).\n129\tBPF LSM must be enabled on the new kernel (`lsm=` includes `bpf`). The GRUB/BIOS boot repair has\n130\tnever been reboot-tested — keep console access ready. If the new kernel has\n131\t`BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SYNC_WAIT` (ioctl 65), add it to `known_management` in `generate-allow.c`;\n132\totherwise remove `subvol_sync_wait_one` from op-storage `delete_by_id`.\n133\t\n134\t**Owner requirement:** kernel upgrades must not break the system. The exact `uname -r` + BTF-hash\n135\tpin makes every upgrade disable the guard and op-storage until a manual rebuild; that has to change\n136\t(e.g. regenerate/verify the allowlist automatically from the installed UAPI during kernel install,\n137\tkeeping the object CO-RE portable) so a XanMod upgrade boots with storage working.\n138\t\n139\t## Open design point: the network belongs in golden (owner, 15:35Z)\n140\t\n141\tOwner: \"the network needs to be part of the golden\" — chicken-and-egg: deploying/repairing a\n142\trelease needs network access, but the network itself ships in the release. Suggested resolution to\n143\tdiscuss: the base system keeps a minimal management path that never depends on a release (eth0 +\n144\tSSH, console as last resort); the release carries the 3tched topology (OVS, Xray/REALITY, WARP,\n145\tprivate 10.0.0.x, decoy path). A release that breaks networking is recovered by booting the previous\n146\tslot or `opdbus.overlay=off`. Not decided.\n147\t\n148\tOwner follow-up: **build the network directly into the golden subvolume** (`/opt/op-dbus/golden`).\n149\tIt is not live until a slot is activated at boot, so base `eth0` + SSH keeps access during the\n150\tbuild. Requires golden to be root-shaped (network files at real paths: `etc/sv/…`, `etc/xray/…`,\n151\t`etc/network/interfaces.d/…`), and the base must not hold competing network files (base wins on\n152\tconflicts) — keep only the management path there; decide NetworkManager's role.\n153\t\n154\t## Update 17:20Z — release slots staged (Claude, not installed)\n155\t\n156\tOwner: ~72 releases/day → live swap, active re-mounted at boot; overlay on a release-owned\n157\tpath (`/opt/op-dbus/current`), not `/`; network stays on the base system with a preinstall\n158\tscript (supersedes the 15:35Z \"network in golden\" note); a separate guard-trusted cgroup like\n159\top-storage for golden releases. Kit, README and install/rollback scripts:\n160\t`/root/btrfs-enforcement-20261013/deployment-release-slots-20261014/`. Source:\n161\t`/srv/git/odbus-btrfs-enforcement-20261013/crates/op-storage/src/bin/op-release.rs`\n162\t(+ `receive_generated` made `pub` in golden.rs). Built, never run. Nothing on the host changed.\n163\tCargo dispatcher needs `CARGO_REAL_BINARY` and the rustup toolchain on PATH (no /usr/bin/cargo).\n164\t\n165\t## Update 18:10Z — Incus installed; STOP for owner's offline repartition (Claude)\n166\tInstalled (owner-approved): release kit (empty slots @release-a/@release-b on root fs), `@incus`\n167\ton sda2 at /var/lib/incus/disks (fstab, no `nofail`!), Incus 6.0.4 with one btrfs pool `3tched`\n168\t(loop image, fsid a1ab7b42…), guard trusts cgroup opdbus-incus for that fsid only. Deleted the\n169\t78 GB vdb recovery images in ~jeremy; space held by hourly set e5c37c9a home snapshot (subvol 283).\n170\tOwner is booting recovery to repartition sda2 for a vector partition and delete files. Owner wants\n171\tno retirement code and every Btrfs issue fixed before continuing. After offline changes, reconcile\n172\top-storage state.json, hourly/pending.json and storage-policy.json pins before it runs again.\n173\tSnowball decision: ledger only, vectors decoupled, no \"timing\" naming in snowball, no timing rotation.\n174\t\n175\t## Update 23:40Z — LVM + guard UUIDs (Claude, from live CD chroot)\n176\t- New VG 3tched-vg spans sdb1, sdb2, sdc5. LVs: root (d53eeac0), swap, cargo 1.39T (328bc09f =\n177\t  the former RECOVERY fs, now also holds a new @cargo-build), vectors 32G (3b3fd476),\n178\t  ct-upgrade 20G (0d7e3795), seed 20G (e9cf9d60, Ubuntu 26.04 root, NOT yet SEEDING).\n179\t- sda2 (083161be) NOT migrated: @opt @git @logs @cargo-build @golden @incus @home still there and\n180\t  in fstab. Owner wants /home moved to the OS (root) LV.\n181\t- Guard: op-storage cgroup now also trusted for vectors, ct-upgrade, cargo (bootstrap-check.sh\n182\t  STORAGE_FSID_VECTORS/UPGRADE/CARGO, guard run trust lines, ready check). Seed: no trust (RO).\n183\t  Manifest rebuilt (11). Backups: /root/btrfs-enforcement-20261013/deployment-release-slots-20261014/\n184\t  before-lvm-uuids-20261014T233056Z/. Untested until boot (live kernel ≠ pinned 6.12.111).\n185\t- fstab /srv/seed pointed at nonexistent ec66acdf → fixed to e9cf9d60.\n186\t- Seed: OS moved into @ (snapshot of top level, originals removed); seed fstab root subvol=@.\n187\t  No GRUB from the Ubuntu install (no i386-pc, install_devices empty).\n188\t- ct-upgrade: empty @ created (empty `data` subvolume left in place).\n189\t- Deferred to the installed system (no double chroot): seed services from\n190\t  deploy/workspace-image (3tchedfs.service, preflight, prepare-lungs-client.sh) need a built\n191\t  threetched-fs + sealed catalog; lungs socket is host-provided per design (owner to confirm);\n192\t  networkmanager-rs source missing (empty dir in all checkouts). Then set the seed flag.\n193\t- op-storage hard-codes RECOVERY_FS=328bc09f (now the cargo LV) — check before it manages cargo.\n194\t\n195\t## Update 2026-10-15 — storage reshuffle, home move, delete fix (Claude, live CD chroot)\n196\t\n197\tOwner decisions:\n198\t- sda (640G) is in `3tched-vg` (PVs: sda2, sdc5). The 1.5T sdb was only for recovery and is being trashed: all of its LVs go, including cargo (and the Qdrant 6335 data on it).\n199\t- `/home` is the `@home` subvolume on the root fs (d53eeac0). It is still its own subvolume.\n200\t- Vectors are a log of the runtime env, a **hash chain**. They are never in the release stream and never in hourly snapshots. They live in persistent RW storage outside releases and are never restored from a snapshot.\n201\t- Qdrant, Cozo and Xray run natively on the root system as runit services, not in Incus. Do not use the staged `/mnt/qdrant-incus/deploy.sh` as-is, because it targets Incus. Suggested and not yet answered: Xray via `chpst` as an unprivileged user with CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE.\n202\t\n203\tDone:\n204\t- System fs 083161be (3tched-system) now lives on LV `3tched-vg/system` (638G, a single segment on sda2). The fs UUID and subvolumes are unchanged; devid is 2.\n205\t- New `@home` (ID 267, UUID 6a879d99-…) is on d53eeac0, and fstab points at it (backup `/etc/fstab.before-home-move-20261015`). The old `@home` (82G) on 083161be is kept until a reboot is validated.\n206\t- Kernel pin: `linux-image-amd64` and 6.12.111 are on apt hold, and GRUB_DEFAULT is set to 6.12.111 (backups `*.before-kernel-pin-20261015`). Pinning only: the requirement that kernel upgrades must not break the guard is still unmet.\n207\t- storage-policy.json: the home member was re-pinned to the new `@home`, with its destination at `/var/lib/opdbus-storage/system-snapshots/home`. The 13 old hourly snapshots were moved, not deleted, to `*/system-snapshots-preserved-20261015/`. state.json was reset. Backups are in `/root/storage-reconcile-home-20261015/`.\n208\t- op-storage delete bug fix: BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SYNC_WAIT returned EPERM. The call was removed from engine.rs, golden.rs and capture.rs, and capture.rs now has a readback check. The binary was rebuilt and installed, and the manifest verifies. The build used cargo directly in the chroot, **not through the dispatcher** (the dispatcher is absent there). Not committed.\n209\t- sdb refs removed from fstab, bootstrap-check.sh and the guard's run file (the pre-LVM versions were restored, and manifest hashes were updated). sdb1 is out of the VG and wiped.\n210\t\n211\tPending:\n212\t- After reboot: lvremove cargo, seed, ct-upgrade and vectors, then vgreduce, pvremove and wipefs sdb2. Cargo was held busy before the reboot by a shell sitting in /media.\n213\t- Reboot validation: /home, kernel 6.12.111, guard, op-storage. The second hourly run tests the delete fix.\n214\t- After validation: delete the old `@home` on 083161be and the 13 preserved snapshots.\n215\t- Open: which Qdrant data set to use (`qdrant-drive-recovery` on 6343, the staged `qdrant-recovered`, or a merge).\n216\t\n217\t## Update 2026-10-15 06:15Z — XanMod installed, bootloader actually updated (Claude, live CD chroot)\n218\t- Previous kernel-pin step edited /etc/default/grub but /boot (sda1) was NOT mounted in the chroot, and\n219\t  sdc's MBR GRUB still loaded a stale Oct-13 config from sdc1. Both disks are MBR with BIOS GRUB (grub-pc).\n220\t- XanMod repo added (key D38D7D1DA1349567ADED882D86F7D09EE734E623, /etc/apt/sources.list.d/xanmod.sources,\n221\t  suite trixie). Installed linux-xanmod-lts-x64v3 → 6.18.56-x64v3-xanmod1 (CPU = x86-64-v3). Not held.\n222\t  Config: BPF_LSM=y, CONFIG_LSM includes bpf, DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y, BTRFS=y; initramfs has lvm + dm-mod.\n223\t  UAPI has BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SYNC_WAIT (ioctl 65).\n224\t- GRUB_DEFAULT → XanMod advanced entry; 6.12.111 + 6.12.73 remain in \"Advanced options\" as fallback.\n225\t  update-grub on sda1; grub-install i386-pc to BOTH sda and sdc (both now load sda1); debconf\n226\t  grub-pc/install_devices lists both disks. Backups: *.before-xanmod-20261015T061435Z.\n227\t- Expected on XanMod boot: guard + op-storage REFUSE to start (bootstrap-check.sh pins uname -r\n228\t  6.12.111 + BTF hash). Next: rebuild guard against 6.18.56 UAPI/BTF, add ioctl 65 to known_management,\n229\t  update pins/manifest — and replace the exact pin with an upgrade-safe check (owner requirement).\n230\t\n231\t## Update 2026-10-15 06:20Z — guard rebuilt for XanMod 6.18.56 (Claude, live CD chroot)\n232\t- Build dir: /root/btrfs-enforcement-20261013/kernel-guard-6.18.56-xanmod/ (original kernel-guard/ untouched).\n233\t  BTF = .BTF section extracted from /boot/vmlinuz (method reproduces the pinned 6.12.111 hash 117c3da3…);\n234\t  XanMod BTF sha256 488c010609b5e98244ddf062cd7bcaf86b17b2a32bc70b369ca3c2a4efd59cb2.\n235\t  UAPI = XanMod include/uapi btrfs.h/btrfs_tree.h sanitized with headers_install.sh's sed stage (no unifdef).\n236\t- Only source change: generate-allow.c adds BTRFS_IOC_SUBVOL_SYNC_WAIT (0x40109441) to known_management\n237\t  (trusted cgroup+FSID only). allow.generated.h differs from the 6.12 build by that one line only.\n238\t- CO-RE relocations of the new guard.bpf.o resolve against BOTH 6.18.56 and 6.12.111 BTF (bpftool gen min_core_btf).\n239\t- Installed guard.bpf.o; bootstrap-check.sh now accepts a list of reviewed (uname -r, BTF sha256) pairs:\n240\t  XanMod 6.18.56 and 6.12.111. Manifest updated (2 lines), verifies. guardctl unchanged.\n241\t  Tested verify_bootstrap with shimmed uname/BTF: both pass, mismatched pair and live 7.0 refused.\n242\t  Backup: /root/btrfs-enforcement-20261013/before-xanmod-guard-20261015T061854Z/.\n243\t- NOT yet tested: actual guard load + op-storage start on XanMod (needs boot). Still an explicit allowlist\n244\t  of kernels — a new kernel needs the same build + one case line; automating that at kernel install\n245\t  (/etc/kernel/postinst.d hook) is the remaining owner requirement.\n246\t\n247\t## Update 2026-10-16 ~20:55Z — Xray native on host, new keys (Claude)\n248\t- Owner: Xray keys are nonconsequential → regenerate; install directly on host (no Incus CT); listen on sockets, not ports.\n249\t- Installed Xray v26.3.27 (repo pin) from GitHub release, zip SHA2-256 23cd9af9…c8ae matched .dgst → /usr/local/bin/xray, geo data /usr/local/share/xray.\n250\t- New key set in /etc/xray/keys (root 0700, files 0600): x25519.txt, mldsa65.txt, client-uuid.txt, short-id.txt, vlessenc.txt, xhttp-path.txt. Never printed.\n251\t- System user `xray` (uid 995). Service /etc/sv/xray (+log, svlogd /var/log/xray), source in repo deploy/runit/xray-native/. Runs chpst -u xray, sockets under /run/ghostbridge/xray/, refuses without a valid /etc/xray/xray_config.json. NOT enabled (no config yet).\n252\t- Verified this build binds a vless/xhttp inbound on a UDS (throwaway config).\n253\t- Old live config: not in git (only deploy/workspace-network/host-xray.json template). In Drive only inside @.tar.zst (22.5 GB root archive, folder 1ziTVXda…); no Drive CLI on host.\n254\t- Decoy still holds the OLD keys; it must get the new private key/shortId/uuid/MLDSA seed/XHTTP encryption before anything connects.\n255\t"}]}
