tion and a 40 GiB upgrade partition.\n\n**Stage 3 (`--prepare-filesystems`): the sealed seed isn't on this host.** The one Codex sealed with `btrfstune -S 1` on Oct 11 is the Ubuntu 26.10 seed `3415d575` on `/dev/sdc2`. There's no `sdc` disk now, and I found no copy of it under `/mnt`. The only seed here is the 10 GiB LV `SDA_SEED` (`8468cc14`), and it isn't that seed:\n- It isn't sealed.\n- It has only the `@` subvolume, none of the six `@agent_*`.\n- It's a stock Ubuntu Studio 26.04 desktop whose fstab still points at the old `e9cf9d60` seed.\n- It has one FUSE unit (`3tchedfs.service`), not two, and stock NetworkManager rather than networkmanager-rs.\n\nI left that seed untouched.\n\nTests haven't been run; that's waiting for you to ask. I've recorded the current state in my HANDOFF row (line 465). The dated HANDOFF entry hasn't been written yet, and nothing is committed.\n\nDecision for you: can `sdc` be reattached, or does a backup of `3415d575` exist (Drive, or another disk)? If not, the 10 GiB `SDA_SEED` LV has to be built up with the 3tched additions and sealed before stage 3 can run."}]}
