{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":739,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:17:53.536Z","uuid":"81ce0136-ecd8-40a0-b309-477f4016b9ea","parentUuid":"0c638c0a-bb7e-48b8-9d0d-4b18314185ad","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On the host, yes. In the seed, no: it mounts only one.\n\n**Host:** two `fuse.3tchedFS` mounts are up:\n- `/run/mounts/3tchedFS`, the OP-DBUS plugins view\n- `/run/mounts/threetched`, the threetched/router view\n\n**Seed (`SDA_SEED` `8468cc14`):** only one is set up.\n- `3tchedfs.service` runs `mount /run/mount/3tchedfs`, which uses the seed's single fstab line: `3tchedFS /run/mount/3tchedfs fuse.3tchedFS noauto,rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,noatime`.\n- The unit shows up under both `/lib` and `/usr/lib` only because `/lib` is a symlink to `/usr/lib` on Ubuntu, so it's the same file.\n- No unit or fstab entry exists for a second (`threetched`) mount inside the guest.\n\nSo the guest is missing the second FUSE mount you expected. That's another sign this LV isn't the seed you had set up on `sdc2`."}]}
