{"source_path":"/home/jeremy/.claude/projects/-srv-git-odbus-verified/f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635.jsonl","source_line":751,"timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:19:28.805Z","uuid":"b860fcc4-9f75-4145-a06a-46337e48291b","parentUuid":"cb4afd4e-a178-43f2-9c7c-2810ca0ade3e","sessionId":"f4c461eb-d25f-4247-9bd7-eddda9ade635","type":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood: the seed is the LV partition mounted at `/run/mount/3tched-seed`, not a sealed seed on another disk.\n\nThe problem is that stage 3 can't sprout a leaf from it as it stands, and the script is right to refuse:\n- **No SEEDING flag.** `btrfs device add` only creates a separate leaf when the seed carries that flag. On an unflagged filesystem, adding the chatbot's partition just makes it part of the seed's own filesystem, so the chatbot's writes land in the seed shared by every leaf. That's why `prepare-instance-disk.sh` stops with \"seed is not sealed\".\n- **Missing members.** The script also requires `@agent_memory`, `@agent_rules`, `@agent_shared`, `@agent_skills`, `@agent_soul` and `@agent_user` in the seed. This partition has only `@`.\n- **About the loop:** the script itself attaches a read-only loop of the seed for each leaf, and the Oct 11 chatbot sprout (HANDOFF line 4507) used one too. The partition stays mounted at `/run/mount/3tched-seed` either way.\n\nGetting this partition ready to sprout from:\n1. Create the six empty `@agent_*` subvolumes in it.\n2. Add anything else the seed should carry before it's frozen, such as the second FUSE mount unit, which it doesn't have yet.\n3. Run `btrfstune -S 1` on it. That needs a brief unmount; it then remounts at `/run/mount/3tched-seed` and stays mounted, read-only, for good.\n4. Re-run stage 3 with `--seed-device /dev/disk/by-uuid/8468cc14-a5e4-409c-96f6-1e157d470ab5`.\n\nShould I do steps 1 and 3 now, or do you want to add more to the seed (like the second FUSE m"}]}
