rified_at_utc\": \"2026-10-05T00:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\nThe caller is responsible for downloading and verifying those artifacts before\ncalling `prepare`. The helper records the downloaded archive's provenance;\nit does not claim to perform the signature or archive verification itself.\n\nBefore metadata preparation, `prepare-lungs-client TOP READ_ONLY_RELEASE`\ninstalls the release's `3tched-fs` client and a public schema-only view in\nthe already writable offline base. It requires a root-controlled read-only\nrelease under `/opt/op-dbus/releases` or `/opt/op-dbus/release-send` and reads\nthe catalog at `usr/share/op-dbus/plugin-blobs`. The receipt distinguishes a\nretained received release from a native source snapshot; a source snapshot is\nnot evidence of receipt or activation. It refuses existing client/view targets and never\ncaptures live SHM or credentials. The guest's enabled `3tchedfs.service` runs\n`mount /run/mount/3tchedfs`, using this `/etc/fstab` entry:\n\n```fstab\n3tchedFS /run/mount/3tchedfs fuse.3tchedFS noauto,rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,noatime 0 0\n```\n\n`noauto` prevents a competing early-boot mount; the enabled service starts it\nafter local filesystems and tmpfiles. `/usr/sbin/mount.fuse.3tchedFS` runs the\nexisting preflight and foreground client under service supervision. A manual\n`mount /run/mount/3tchedfs` also stays in the foreground. Unsupported mount\noptions are rejected rather than silently ignored. Runtime prerequisites remain\n`/dev/fuse`, the lungs socket, sealed catalog, schema-only view and empty state\ndirectory. Offline configuration checks do not prove an identity-bound mount\nor a successful boot.\n\nHost agents use a separate projection of the same blobs; no copied schema or\nsynchronization layer is required. A guest may also serve its MCP clients with:\n\n```sh\n3tched-fs --store /usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-view mcp \\\n  --state /usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-empty-state \\\n  --lungs-socket /run/3tched-lungs.socket --all\n```\n\nOmitting `--lungs-session` selects `BindCurrentContainer`; the bridge derives\nthe caller from its kernel peer process and the committed native container.\nThe socket accepts connections with mode `0666` beneath a root-owned `0755`\ndirectory. Connection permission conveys no plugin authority: binding and\nevery operation revalidate the native identity and existing grants. Explicit\nsession binding is restricted to root in the bridge's host namespaces.\n\nIncus shares only the host's dedicated `/run/opdbus/lungs` directory, read-only,\nat the same guest path. The installed tmpfiles rule `3tched-lungs.conf` creates\nthe guest-local `/run/3tched-lungs.socket` entrypoint pointing to\n`/run/opdbus/lungs/lungs.sock` after `/run` is mounted. The public entrypoint is\nnot a second listener. Directory binding keeps socket replacement visible\nafter a bridge restart; binding the socket inode alone does not. Never bind\nthe host's entire `/run` to provide the public entrypoint.\n\nFor a headless seed, keep display-manager packages installed but mask the\ninstalled display-manager unit and `display-manager.service`, and select\n`multi-user.target` as the default. A network manager's enablement must follow\nthe actual selected adapter's dependencies, not a similarly named project's\ndocumentation. The loopback relay and host internet carrier are separate\nprerequisites; a D-Bus socket alone does not establish internet access.\n\n`verify TOP` is the pre-seal check. It validates the exact seven Btrfs sibling\nnames and mount layout, metadata schema and artifact hashes, the complete\noffline dpkg installed-package inventory, hashes and symlink targets for the\ncritical OS/init files, and neutral machine identity defaults. It reads the\ntarget tree as files and never runs binaries from it. The package component\ntable marks each selected component present or missing based on the offline\ndpkg database; a missing optional component is reported as missing rather\nthan inferred from filenames or treated as installed.\n\n`verify-metadata TOP` is for later checks of a writable sprout. It validates\nthe metadata schema, pinned layout, and all metadata artifact hashes, then\nprints a stable one-line JSON receipt containing `schema_version`,\n`release_id`, `layout`, and `manifest_sha256`. It deliberately does not compare\ninstalled package versions, critical OS files, hostname, machine ID, or\nper-leaf contents, so ordinary guest updates and identity changes do not\ninvalidate the base metadata receipt. The caller should pin these exact fields\nin its provisioning receipt and compare them on subsequent checks.\n\n`inspect TOP` performs full verification and prints the manifest. The\nmanifest's critical hash inventory is deliberately limited to `/etc/os-release`,\n`/etc/fstab`, the systemd executable, and `/usr/sbin/init`; it excludes\nhostname, machine ID, SSH keys, credentials, agent data, persistence contents,\nand runtime state. `@agent_user/persist` is an ordinary directory, not another\nsubvolume. The guest-owned `/run/mount/3tchedfs` FUSE mount and per-boot\nprivate state under `/dev/shm` are runtime mounts, not seed contents. The\n`3tched-lungs` Incus profile supplies `/run` as tmpfs and mounts the host's\ndedicated `/run/opdbus/lungs` directory read-only at the same guest path.\nSocket permissions and per-connection identity authentication remain the\nresponsibility of the socket service.\n\nThe base should remain unchanged while any sprout depends on it. Seed recovery\ntools and an external copy of the manifest must remain available outside the\nseed so recovery does not depend on mounting the base itself. The helper never\nseals or changes the filesystem read-only; the caller owns that lifecycle\ntransition.\n\nThe isolated shell fixture test is `tests/test-op-identity-image.sh`. It uses\nordinary temporary directories and a mocked `btrfs` listing; it does not mount\nor modify a filesystem device.\n=====\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Offline image preparation; never mounts, unseals or starts a guest/service.\nset -euo pipefail\nfail() { printf 'prepare-lungs-client: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\n[[ $# == 2 && $(id -u) == 0 ]] || fail 'usage (host root): TOP READ_ONLY_RELEASE'\ntop=$1 release=$2\n[[ $top == /* && $(realpath -e \"$top\") == \"$top\" && $top != / ]] || fail 'noncanonical image top'\n[[ $(realpath -e \"$release\") == \"$release\" ]] || fail 'noncanonical release path'\ncase \"$release\" in\n    /opt/op-dbus/releases/*) release_kind=received-release ;;\n    /opt/op-dbus/release-send/*) release_kind=source-snapshot ;;\n    *) fail 'expected retained received release or native release-send snapshot' ;;\nesac\nparent=$release\nwhile :; do\n    [[ $(stat -c %u \"$parent\") == 0 ]] || fail 'release path is not root-owned'\n    mode=$(stat -c %a \"$parent\")\n    (( (8#$mode & 022) == 0 )) || fail 'release path is writable by another owner'\n    [[ $parent == / ]] && break\n    parent=$(dirname -- \"$parent\")\ndone\n[[ $(btrfs property get \"$release\" ro) == ro=true ]] || fail 'release must be read-only'\n[[ $(findmnt -rn -M \"$top\" -o FSTYPE) == btrfs ]] || fail 'image top must be an existing Btrfs mount'\ncase \",$(findmnt -rn -M \"$top\" -o OPTIONS),\" in *,rw,*) ;; *) fail 'image must already be in authorized writable maintenance' ;; esac\nguest=$top/@\n[[ -d $guest && ! -L $guest ]] || fail 'missing guest root'\nassets=$(cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\nclient=$release/bin/3tched-fs\ncatalog=$release/usr/share/op-dbus/plugin-blobs\n[[ -f $client && ! -L $client && -x $client && -d $catalog && ! -L $catalog ]] || fail 'release client or sealed public catalog absent'\nfor asset in 3tchedfs.service 3tchedfs-mount-preflight 3tched-lungs.conf mount.fuse.3tchedFS 3tchedfs.fstab; do\n    [[ -f $assets/$asset ]] || fail \"guest mount asset is absent: $asset\"\ndone\n[[ -z $(find \"$catalog\" -type l -print -quit) ]] || fail 'sealed catalog contains a symlink'\nfor rel in usr usr/sbin usr/local usr/local/bin usr/local/libexec usr/local/libexec/3tched usr/lib usr/lib/systemd usr/lib/systemd/system usr/lib/tmpfiles.d etc etc/systemd etc/systemd/system etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants usr/share usr/share/op-dbus; do\n    path=$guest/$rel\n    if [[ ! -e $path && ! -L $path ]]; then mkdir -m 0755 \"$path\"; fi\n    [[ -d $path && ! -L $path && $(stat -c %u \"$path\") == 0 ]] || fail \"unsafe image directory: $rel\"\ndone\nstore=$guest/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-view\nempty=$guest/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-empty-state\nguest_catalog=$guest/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-catalog\nunit=$guest/usr/lib/systemd/system/3tchedfs.service\nunit_link=$guest/etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/3tchedfs.service\npreflight=$guest/usr/local/libexec/3tched/3tchedfs-mount-preflight\nsocket_link_config=$guest/usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/3tched-lungs.conf\nmount_helper=$guest/usr/sbin/mount.fuse.3tchedFS\nfstab=$guest/etc/fstab\n[[ -f $fstab && ! -L $fstab && $(stat -c %u \"$fstab\") == 0 ]] || fail 'unsafe or absent guest fstab'\nif findmnt --fstab --tab-file \"$fstab\" -rn -o TARGET | grep -iFxq /run/mount/3tchedfs; then\n    fail 'guest fstab already declares a 3tchedFS mount; inspect before replacing'\nfi\n[[ ! -e $store && ! -L $store && ! -e $empty && ! -L $empty && ! -e $guest_catalog && ! -L $guest_catalog ]] || fail 'lungs client view or catalog already prepared; inspect existing image'\n[[ ! -e $guest/usr/local/bin/3tched-fs && ! -L $guest/usr/local/bin/3tched-fs ]] || fail 'client already exists; inspect before replacing'\nfor path in \"$unit\" \"$unit_link\" \"$preflight\" \"$socket_link_config\" \"$mount_helper\"; do\n    [[ ! -e $path && ! -L $path ]] || fail \"guest mount service already exists: $path\"\ndone\ninstall -m 0755 \"$client\" \"$guest/usr/local/bin/3tched-fs\"\ninstall -d -m 0755 \"$empty\" \"$store\"\n# Only schema/catalog material enters the base; live SHM and SID1 never do.\n\"$client\" --store \"$store\" capture --schema-only --catalog \"$catalog\" --state \"$empty\"\ncp -a -- \"$catalog\" \"$guest_catalog\"\nfind \"$store\" -type d -exec chmod 0755 {} +\nfind \"$store\" -type f -exec chmod 0644 {} +\nfind \"$guest_catalog\" -type d -exec chmod 0755 {} +\nfind \"$guest_catalog\" -type f -exec chmod 0644 {} +\n[[ -z $(find \"$empty\" -mindepth 1 -print -quit) ]] || fail 'schema capture populated state unexpectedly'\ncmp \"$client\" \"$guest/usr/local/bin/3tched-fs\"\ncmp \"$catalog/.manifest.json\" \"$guest_catalog/.manifest.json\"\ninstall -m 0755 \"$assets/3tchedfs-mount-preflight\" \"$preflight\"\ninstall -m 0644 \"$assets/3tchedfs.service\" \"$unit\"\ninstall -m 0644 \"$assets/3tched-lungs.conf\" \"$socket_link_config\"\ninstall -m 0755 \"$assets/mount.fuse.3tchedFS\" \"$mount_helper\"\nprintf '\\n' >> \"$fstab\"\ncat \"$assets/3tchedfs.fstab\" >> \"$fstab\"\nln -s /usr/lib/systemd/system/3tchedfs.service \"$unit_link\"\njq -n --arg release \"${release##*/}\" --arg release_kind \"$release_kind\" \\\n    --arg client_sha256 \"$(sha256sum \"$client\" | cut -d ' ' -f1)\" \\\n    --arg catalog_sha256 \"$(sha256sum \"$catalog/.manifest.json\" | cut -d ' ' -f1)\" \\\n    '{release:$release,release_kind:$release_kind,client_sha256:$client_sha256,catalog_manifest_sha256:$catalog_sha256,\n      socket:\"/run/3tched-lungs.socket\",binding:\"BindCurrentContainer\",state:\"empty\",\n      mount_service:\"3tchedfs.service\",mountpoint:\"/run/mount/3tchedfs\",mount_table:\"/etc/fstab\",\n      command:[\"3tched-fs\",\"--store\",\"/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-view\",\"mcp\",\"--state\",\n       \"/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-empty-state\",\"--lungs-socket\",\"/run/3tched-lungs.socket\",\"--all\"]}' \\\n    > \"$guest/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-client.json\"\nchmod 0644 \"$guest/usr/share/op-dbus/lungs-client.json\"\nprintf 'Prepared one guest 3tchedFS systemd mount from %s %s.\\n' \"$release_kind\" \"${release##*/}\"","is_error":false}]}
